Action Against Hunger is currently looking to fill the role of Head of Department Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability, and Learning (MEAL), who will be responsible to lead the successful implementation of monitoring, evaluation, accountability and learning systems for programs and projects, both new and established, ensuring efficiency in project deliverables. The MEAL HOD is also to provide technical support to the MEAL team on the implementation of an effective system to monitor progress, outcomes, impacts and successes of project activities and performance at all levels and also required to act as the technical advisor for the department.
Reporting to:
Deputy Country Director Programmes
Proposed start date:
April 2025
Work location:
Abuja, FCT
Key Responsibilities
:
Ensuring contextualized MEAL systems are developed to guide project implementation in compliance with ACF’s MEAL Guidelines and Minimum Requirements for MEAL;
